1
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,200
Don't jump!

2
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,759
Think of your family!

3
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:39,200
Think of your wife!

4
00:00:46,439 --> 00:00:47,280
Who am I?

5
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,079
Where am I?

6
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,359
My life...

7
00:00:51,359 --> 00:00:53,240
How did it come to this?

8
00:00:57,479 --> 00:00:58,119
And...

9
00:00:58,679 --> 00:00:59,719
Not just once.

10
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,079
A second time.

11
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:02,960
A third time.

12
00:01:04,719 --> 00:01:05,359
Four times.

13
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:07,560
This one doesn't count.

14
00:01:07,959 --> 00:01:08,640
Five times.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:10,480
Six times.

16
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,439
Seven times.

17
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:12,319
Eight times.

18
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,480
I don't get it either.

19
00:01:16,239 --> 00:01:17,640
How did things get so messed up?

20
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:19,159
Just why?

21
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,000
Is the universe just out to get me?

22
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,400
Why won't this open?

23
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,159
Why can't I get in?

24
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,520
If you could get in,

25
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,280
what would they need us for?

26
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,680
Bro, can you make an exception?

27
00:02:54,599 --> 00:02:56,000
I just need to grab some personal stuff.

28
00:02:56,039 --> 00:02:57,039
I'll be right out.

29
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,280
G-get lost, now.

30
00:02:58,479 --> 00:03:00,039
If you keep messing around here,

31
00:03:00,039 --> 00:03:01,159
believe me, I'll beat the crap out of you.

32
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,159
Wait, I'm the author of this book.

33
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,439
Why won't you let me in?

34
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:13,719
Hello, Ms. Jin.

35
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:18,319
Ms. Jin! Ms. Jin!

36
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:19,639
So many people.

37
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,520
Excuse me.

38
00:03:21,039 --> 00:03:21,719
Just give me half a minute.

39
00:03:22,199 --> 00:03:23,599
My keycard isn't working.

40
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,400
Let me introduce you.

41
00:03:26,479 --> 00:03:27,879
This here is Mike.

42
00:03:27,879 --> 00:03:29,400
While studying abroad in the US,

43
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,879
he majored in health and nutrition.

44
00:03:30,879 --> 00:03:32,080
And a healthy lifestyle is exactly

45
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,000
the current trend in urban living.

46
00:03:34,159 --> 00:03:35,479
So we plan to have Mike

47
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:36,879
serve as the group's brand ambassador.

48
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:37,840
Hey, man.

49
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:40,919
Easy, easy.

50
00:03:41,319 --> 00:03:42,439
So he's our colleague now?

51
00:03:42,719 --> 00:03:44,039
He used to be, but not anymore.

52
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:46,120
What? What do you mean not a colleague?

53
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,319
Not a colleague? No, no.

54
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,159
We realized that

55
00:03:48,159 --> 00:03:50,000
no matter how we fake your trending stats,

56
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,120
you don't have any real fans.

57
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,840
Your book's content is definitely out of touch with the market.

58
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,120
Young people nowadays

59
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,759
aren't into that cheesy self-help stuff.

60
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,599
That's a flaw in our strategy as well.

61
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,759
But that's completely normal.

62
00:03:59,919 --> 00:04:00,560
It's business.

63
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:01,479
Business.

64
00:04:04,599 --> 00:04:05,599
Not a single real fan?

65
00:04:05,599 --> 00:04:06,560
Could there be a mistake?

66
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,000
Why don't you take another look?

67
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:10,400
Also, I just want to go up and get...

68
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,879
Why don't you look for another job?

69
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,560
No, I just want to grab my things.

70
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:25,800
We're done working together.

71
00:04:29,319 --> 00:04:30,920
She only hired me because of you.

72
00:04:31,399 --> 00:04:32,160
Now that she's giving up on you,

73
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,160
she's dumping me too.

74
00:04:33,399 --> 00:04:34,160
Just like that.

75
00:04:34,319 --> 00:04:35,879
Look, at her level,

76
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:37,639
all she wants is emotional satisfaction.

77
00:04:37,639 --> 00:04:39,480
You should learn from Mike.

78
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,600
He used to just be

79
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,519
a gym membership salesman.

80
00:04:41,519 --> 00:04:43,519
Can't you just move forward?

81
00:04:44,959 --> 00:04:46,480
With a company as big as ours,

82
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:49,120
isn't there anywhere I can pitch in?

83
00:04:49,519 --> 00:04:51,240
Can the newbies even make coffee right?

84
00:04:52,279 --> 00:04:53,720
Besides, I'm still a

85
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,079
deputy editor, after all.

86
00:04:55,399 --> 00:04:56,040
Haowen.

87
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:59,120
About that deputy editor thing... corporate didn't approve it.

88
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:00,839
Given your current situation,

89
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:02,680
if you still want to publish your poems,

90
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,639
your best shortcut is still to woo Jin Furong.

91
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,920
What exactly happened between you two?

92
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,480
You offended her,

93
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,319
and you're putting me in a really tough spot.

94
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:30,600
Success

95
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:32,720
is about having worked hard,

96
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,399
struggled,

97
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,319
and persevered.

98
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:39,199
Even if the ending isn't that perfect,

99
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,279
you still have the courage to face the future.

100
00:05:42,279 --> 00:05:44,000
Have you no shame, Fang Haowen?

101
00:05:44,839 --> 00:05:46,360
You're an intellectual.

102
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,079
So what if I'm an intellectual?!

103
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,439
I've lost my love.

104
00:05:49,439 --> 00:05:50,720
I can't just throw away my career too!

105
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,920
I'm at a complete dead end.

106
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,199
What good is saving face?

107
00:05:53,399 --> 00:05:54,800
Tell me, what's the use of it?!

108
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,519
I just want you to have a little dignity.

109
00:05:56,519 --> 00:05:57,240
I don't need it!

110
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,720
At least be true to your own conscience!

111
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,399
I can't!

112
00:05:59,959 --> 00:06:00,800
Not even a little!

113
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,720
Slap me in the face if you've got the guts!

114
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:03,879
I'll really slap you!

115
00:06:03,879 --> 00:06:04,439
Do it!

116
00:06:13,279 --> 00:06:14,920
Which one of you is scanning the code?

117
00:06:24,639 --> 00:06:25,399
Furong!

118
00:06:27,399 --> 00:06:28,160
Furong!

119
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,199
Rong'er!

120
00:07:08,879 --> 00:07:10,279
Are you off work yet?

121
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,759
I-I-I... I w-w-wanted...

122
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:14,920
...to talk to you about something.

123
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:25,519
Can't drive any further. Just park here.

124
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,600
Baby, come on. Easy, easy, easy.

125
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,680
Park here, park here, park here.

126
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:30,720
Park wherever you want.

127
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,519
Alright.

128
00:07:32,199 --> 00:07:33,319
You can also park over there.

129
00:07:34,439 --> 00:07:35,199
Or park right here.

130
00:07:35,399 --> 00:07:36,240
Okay.

131
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,519
I'm telling you,

132
00:07:37,879 --> 00:07:39,120
you didn't drink earlier.

133
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,759
When we get back, this whole bottle is yours.

134
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:09,360
Wait a sec.

135
00:08:10,199 --> 00:08:11,040
I'll close it.

136
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,000
Close it.

137
00:08:20,639 --> 00:08:21,600
Babe! Babe!

138
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,279
Grab me some pajamas, babe.

139
00:08:23,279 --> 00:08:24,240
Okay, baby.

140
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:28,839
Baby, you have so many pajamas. Which one?

141
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,360
Want me to come out and help you pick?

142
00:08:31,399 --> 00:08:33,480
Never mind. Just pick one for me.

143
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,120
Alright.

144
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,240
I'm thirsty. I want some water.

145
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:40,840
Thirsty, huh?

146
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:04,200
Babe, champagne's here.

147
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,159
Baby, you didn't bring me a glass.

148
00:09:06,159 --> 00:09:06,919
Where are the glasses?

149
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:08,799
On the cart on the left.

150
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,159
Okay, babe.

151
00:09:17,519 --> 00:09:18,480
Coming.

152
00:09:23,679 --> 00:09:25,639
Baby, I'm heading out first.

153
00:09:25,919 --> 00:09:27,240
Make sure you wash up nicely.

154
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,399
Xiaobao, turn off the lights.

155
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,200
Why are the lights off?

156
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,480
Xiaobao, turn on the lights.

157
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:46,919
Grant me a peach blossom haven, a haven...

158
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:49,480
Don't leave me heartbroken...

159
00:09:49,879 --> 00:09:52,440
With no one to comfort me...

160
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,600
Babe.

161
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,360
You're taking so long. You meanie.

162
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,000
Come here, babe.

163
00:10:02,399 --> 00:10:03,039
Baby...

164
00:10:06,159 --> 00:10:06,879
Hold on, hold on.

165
00:10:07,399 --> 00:10:07,919
Who's there?

166
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,919
Who is it? What was that noise?

167
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:14,879
Who's there?

168
00:10:14,879 --> 00:10:16,200
Xiaobao, please turn off the lights.

169
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:17,600
Who's there?

170
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,480
Who is it?

171
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,039
Stop right there!

172
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:20,879
You!

173
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,000
Catch him! Catch him!

174
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,120
Xiaobao, turn on the lights!

175
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:40,960
Fang Haowen!

176
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,720
I wanted to surprise you.

177
00:10:51,879 --> 00:10:52,720
It's called a scare.

178
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,200
I almost called the cops.

179
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,519
You're even wearing a dog collar, huh?

180
00:10:59,120 --> 00:10:59,759
Hand it over.

181
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:04,759
Look, let me just say...

182
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:05,799
My phone...

183
00:11:06,759 --> 00:11:08,960
is on the sink in your bathroom.

184
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,120
Go get it for him.

185
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,960
Please, can I just ask...

186
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:13,320
what exactly did I do wrong?

187
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,799
Can you give me one more chance?

188
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:15,639
Let me ask you something.

189
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,480
How did you get in?

190
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,799
Last time I brought you home...

191
00:11:18,799 --> 00:11:19,799
you told me the passcode.

192
00:11:19,799 --> 00:11:20,600
Let me tell you something.

193
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,799
You can never come in here again.

194
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,720
Or I'll call the cops on you.

195
00:11:25,879 --> 00:11:27,000
You also told me...

196
00:11:28,039 --> 00:11:30,159
you said you admired my talent.

197
00:11:30,159 --> 00:11:31,759
You have absolutely no talent.

198
00:11:32,879 --> 00:11:35,240
So were you admiring my body?

199
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,240
If you didn't admire my talent,

200
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,600
why would you let me write a book?

201
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,960
I could've gotten anyone to write a book.

202
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,120
If it weren't for me,

203
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,840
would your crappy book have been published?

204
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,799
Furong.

205
00:11:46,799 --> 00:11:48,200
You... you can insult me, but...

206
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,559
don't insult my work.

207
00:11:51,559 --> 00:11:52,720
Bullshit. Your work?

208
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,000
That is my work.

209
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,200
Have you ever been successful?

210
00:11:55,679 --> 00:11:57,159
How many successful people have you interviewed?

211
00:11:57,159 --> 00:11:58,440
And you write "What Is Success"?

212
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,360
Do you really think

213
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:00,799
you're on the same level as them?

214
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:02,559
You're a nobody.

215
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:03,559
Without me,

216
00:12:03,559 --> 00:12:04,600
you couldn't publish a book.

217
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,000
That book is mine.

218
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,480
Th... That's the book I wrote.

219
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,840
How could it be yours?

220
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,039
You wanted to write poetry.

221
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,279
I made you write a textbook.

222
00:12:14,279 --> 00:12:15,279
The textbook belongs to our company.

223
00:12:15,279 --> 00:12:16,360
The copyright is mine.

224
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,480
But the content is mine, isn't it?

225
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,440
I got someone to publish it for you.

226
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,720
Got someone to fake the stats for you.

227
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,480
Hired fake fans for your press conference.

228
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,799
Even the inscription on the cover...

229
00:12:23,799 --> 00:12:25,080
I wrote it for you, didn't I?

230
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,159
I practically held your hand to type!

231
00:12:27,679 --> 00:12:28,679
Write, my ass!

232
00:12:28,759 --> 00:12:29,440
It's been half a year, right?

233
00:12:29,759 --> 00:12:31,200
I hyped that book up so much,

234
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,600
and now look at your conversion rate!

235
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:33,440
And why is that?

236
00:12:33,759 --> 00:12:34,759
Because your writing sucks!

237
00:12:34,759 --> 00:12:35,639
You're useless!

238
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,519
You have absolutely no talent!

239
00:12:42,879 --> 00:12:43,799
Who do you think you're relying on?

240
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:45,600
Turns out you're so ugly on the inside.

241
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:46,919
Just like you are on the outside.

242
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,799
I've been sick of you for a long time.

243
00:12:49,799 --> 00:12:50,679
You know that?

244
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,600
And you wanted me to kiss you.

245
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:56,600
Truly disgusting.

246
00:12:57,279 --> 00:12:58,080
You...

247
00:12:58,879 --> 00:13:00,200
are a bloated mess.

248
00:13:06,879 --> 00:13:07,639
Get the hell out!

249
00:13:09,279 --> 00:13:10,399
And you, listen to me.

250
00:13:10,399 --> 00:13:11,840
Change the passcode immediately.

251
00:13:12,279 --> 00:13:13,600
Pick any random numbers.

252
00:13:13,879 --> 00:13:15,200
Don't let him in ever again.

253
00:13:15,919 --> 00:13:17,519
If you let him in again,

254
00:13:17,519 --> 00:13:18,519
I'll fire you.

255
00:13:18,919 --> 00:13:19,879
Got it?

256
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:46,360
Please park shared bikes in designated areas.

257
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,320
Can't you drive?!

258
00:14:00,519 --> 00:14:01,600
Where are your manners?!

259
00:14:02,159 --> 00:14:03,679
Did the rain get into your brain?!

260
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,879
Thinking about finding a partner?

261
00:14:43,159 --> 00:14:44,120
Do you have any criteria?

262
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:44,720
Yeah, I do.

263
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:46,519
I don't care how successful

264
00:14:46,519 --> 00:14:47,519
my partner is.

265
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:49,120
As long as he loves me, and only me,

266
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,399
that's enough for me.

267
00:14:50,399 --> 00:14:52,240
She ran off with that travel agency boss.

268
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:00,320
We realized that

269
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,200
no matter how we fake your trending stats,

270
00:15:02,279 --> 00:15:03,519
you don't have any real fans.

271
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,639
I knew it! How could that be?

272
00:15:52,639 --> 00:15:53,799
Not a single real fan.

273
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,440
Your book's content is definitely out of touch with the market.

274
00:15:57,639 --> 00:15:58,639
Young people nowadays

275
00:15:58,639 --> 00:16:00,399
aren't into that cheesy self-help stuff.

276
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,639
Since my first book wasn't what I really intended,

277
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:10,480
I'll write one that fixes my past mistakes.

278
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:12,600
A book free from constraints.

279
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:14,279
A truly free book.

280
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:17,159
A book that mocks hustle culture.

281
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:25,039
Wang Fuxiang.

282
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,320
Bye, Haozi.

283
00:16:29,799 --> 00:16:31,720
I'm leaving this filthy place.

284
